@title Product Design Principles
@subtitle For every customer-facing app at Fathom Bank
@author Design Systems team, Fathom Bank

These principles were agreed in a workshop with 26 designers and engineers on 2026-09-17. They apply to all customer-facing apps, and every design review should be measured against them.

## Clarity over cleverness
Customers come to us to move and manage money, not to admire an interface. When there is a choice between a plain label and a clever one, choose the plain one, especially wherever money moves.
- **Do:** label buttons with the action.
- **Avoid:** icons without text for money movement.

## Show the money
Customers should never be surprised by what something costs. Fees, rates and totals belong on screen early enough to change the customer's mind.
- **Do:** show fees before confirmation.
- **Avoid:** revealing fees on the final screen.

## Forgive mistakes
People tap the wrong thing, and a banking app should make that cheap to fix. Undo should be easy and immediate, not a separate process.
- **Do:** allow undo for 10 seconds after a transfer is scheduled.
- **Avoid:** making cancellation a phone call.

## Accessible by default
Accessibility is part of the design from the first sketch, not a pass at the end. Every customer should be able to read and act on every screen.
- **Do:** meet a contrast ratio of 4.5 to 1.
- **Avoid:** relying on color alone for status.

## Calm, not urgent
Financial decisions deserve time. We give customers the facts they need and let them decide at their own pace, without manufactured pressure.
- **Do:** state plain deadlines.
- **Avoid:** countdown timers that push decisions.

---

> If a customer has to read it twice, we wrote it wrong.
> — Ines Albrecht, Head of Design

! Disagreements with a principle go to the monthly design council, not to individual reviews.
